WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:13,550
Do you have any thoughts on the signature test? I thought I read that it picks up

00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:18,830
remaining circulating tumor cells that are dead from the original tumor.

00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:28,540
Well, the signature test is picking up DNA, circulated tumor DNA. Is it picking up dead

00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:35,340
to circulate tumor cells? No, not to my knowledge. It's picking up circulated tumor cells that

00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:41,260
to circulate tumor cells that are not dead. Is that a good thing to measure?

00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:49,740
Well, some people use it as a measurement of whether the person is doing better or worse,

00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:57,100
so they're doing a signature test. The measure, if the person has a decrease in

00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:03,340
circulated tumor cells, then the practitioner may interpret that by saying the patient is doing

00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:08,460
better. If they have an increase in circulated tumor cells, the practitioner may interpret that

00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:16,140
as the patient is doing worse. However, if you really think about the physiology of that,

00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:25,920
to me, that doesn't quite, and the reason it isn't because a cancer doesn't give off,

00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:32,080
there's no data that says a cancer gives out more circulated tumor cells when it has, as it's

00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:41,040
growing. There's times that it gives off more circulated tumor cells, but it doesn't necessarily,

00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:46,160
it's not a one-to-one equation that the cancer is growing, nor is it a one-to-one correlation that

00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:52,560
a decrease in circulated tumor cells mean the cancer is dying. So I don't see value in doing

00:01:52,560 --> 00:02:01,520
the signature test because the data, it's just confusing. It doesn't give us adequate data to say

00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:09,680
the person is doing better or worse. Again, you do a test if it's giving you data on how you're

00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:17,200
going to change the treatment of the patient. If it's not giving you adequate data,

00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:25,200
objectively whether the person is doing better or worse or needs a change in the treatment plan

00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:32,000
that I don't see any value in spedding the money and running the test. That's why I don't run that test.

00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:39,600
So that's my opinion. I don't think it's adequate objective data that would, that would warn it be

00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:48,000
changing the treatment plan on a patient.

